# Naming

## Language

- Identifiers, file and folder names, comments, action types, event names and docs are English.
- German domain nouns are allowed for product concepts where they are the established term: `dienststelle`, `sicht`, `kennzahl`, `stichtag`, `jahr`. Do not use German (or Dutch) for technical words: `bevestigSelectie`, `auswahlSpeichern` are wrong; `confirmSelection`, `saveSelection` are right.
- User-facing (German) text lives in label config (the module's `config.js` or `_KDB.config.labels`), not in literals scattered through logic.
- Persisted keys and values keep their current spelling even when it breaks these rules (frozen contract).

## Identifiers

- Functions and variables `camelCase`; real constants `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`; constructors `PascalCase`.
- Functions are verb + noun: `readActiveTabId`, `buildHeaderChrome`, `applyFilterCommit`, `syncFooterView`. Prefer precise verbs (`read`, `build`, `render`, `place`, `sync`, `apply`, `commit`, `restore`, `bind`, `create`, `remove`, `parse`, `validate`). Avoid `handle`, `do`, `process`, `manage`, `update`, `change`.
- Booleans: `is*`, `has*`, `can*`, `should*`, `did*`; no negative names (`isNotReady`).
- Selectors: `read*` (`readSelectedWidgetId(_KDB)`). Owner-internal writers: `set*` / `write*`.
- Action types: `<module>/<intent>` (`kdbControl/toggleLaunchpad`, `filters/applyFilter`, `history/commitStep`). No bare `set`, `update`, `change`.
- Event names: see `events.mdc`. New error codes: `<MODULE>_<WHAT>` in `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`; existing codes keep their spelling (see `error-handling.mdc`).
- Existing convention: AMD import bindings and parameters received from other files carry a leading underscore (`_KDB`, `_tabsSelectors`, `_options`); locally built values and inline callback parameters do not. `_KDB` is the only underscore global.

## Files and folders

- Template files have fixed names: `index.js`, `state.js`, `selectors.js`, `view.js`, `effects.js`, `config.js`, `history.js`, `restore.js`, `tabMutation.js`, `events.js` (see `feature-structure.mdc`).
- Other files are named for the concept they hold (`binding.js`, `drillthrough.js`, `legend.js`), or verb + noun for a single job (`buildLaunchpadTabs.js`).
- Folder names are nouns for domains (`binding/`, `restore/`, `primitives/`).
- Forbidden vague names: `helpers`, `common`, `misc`, `manager`, `shared`, `stuff`, and overflow suffixes `Support`, `Helpers`, `Internals`, `Core` (as in `applyRestoreSelectionCore.js`).
- New and refactored code does not use the magic entry names `__controller` or `__orchestrator`; the existing `__orchestrator<M>.js` files that `KDB.js` imports keep their names until Phase 2. Do not mass-rename `handle*` or `__controller` outside a module you are refactoring.
- Rule files: `kebab-case.mdc`.
